        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li><strong>Right to Access &amp; Copies:</strong> Obtain a summary of your personal data and readable copies of clinical charts/radiographs (clinical records provided within <strong>72 hours</strong> per DCI norms; full data summaries within <strong>15 business days</strong>).</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Correction &amp; Updating:</strong> Request correction of inaccurate, incomplete, or outdated personal details.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Erasure:</strong> Request deletion of website inquiries, WhatsApp chat histories, or non-statutory personal data once the purpose is fulfilled. <em>(Mandatory medical and tax records are locked from active use until statutory Indian retention periods expire.)</em></li>
          <li><strong>Right to Withdraw Consent:</strong> Opt out of WhatsApp reminders, ABHA linking, testimonials, or cookies at any time.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Nominate (DPDP Act, Sec. 14):</strong> Nominate a trusted individual to exercise your data rights on your behalf in case of death or incapacity.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Data Portability &amp; Objection:</strong> Receive digital clinical summaries and radiographs in standard machine-readable formats (PDF/DICOM/ABDM) and object to non-essential processing.</li>
