        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-extrabold text-brand-darkbrown">10. Data Breach Notification Protocol</h2>
        <p>In alignment with <strong>DPDP Rules, 2025 (Rule 7)</strong>, <strong>CERT-In Directions, 2022</strong>, <strong>GDPR</strong>, and the <strong>FTC Health Breach Notification Rule</strong>:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li><strong>Immediate Containment:</strong> Suspected security incidents are immediately isolated and investigated.</li>
          <li><strong>Regulatory Reporting:</strong> Reportable cyber incidents are notified to <strong>CERT-In within 6 hours</strong> of detection. Personal data breaches are reported to the <strong>Data Protection Board of India (DPBI)</strong> via initial intimation without delay, followed by a detailed report within <strong>72 hours</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Patient Notification:</strong> Every affected patient is notified without delay in plain, clear language via registered phone/WhatsApp/email, outlining the nature of the breach, potential consequences, mitigation measures taken, recommended protective steps, and Grievance Officer contact details.</li>
